Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:32:20 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] phyFLEX-stm32mp2 M33 OpenAMP TTY echo example:
 stm32cubemp2 v1.3.2

   The default OpenAMP_TTY_echo example has the following behavior:

   - creates two virtual UART channels between Linux and the Cortex-M33.
   - exposes these channels as /dev/ttyRPMSG0 and /dev/ttyRPMSG1 in Linux.
   - prints received messages on the M33 console.
   - sends each message back to Linux on the same channel.

   The example largely works as-is on the phyFLEX-STM32MP257 Development Kit.
   Here we are making the M33's replies easier to identify and fixing the
   example's compatibility issue with newer CMake versions:

   - added a "M33 Responds: " prefix to replies to Linux.
   - prints only the original received text through UART5.
   - bounds console printing by the received message length rather than
     assuming the RPMsg data is null-terminated.
   - reserves space for the reply prefix within the RPMsg payload limit.

   The bundled libmetal build script requests CMake 3.0.2 compatibility,
   which CMake 4.x no longer supports (STM32CubeIDE 2.2.0 comes with
   CMake 4.3.1. so this required a fix). Added
   -DCMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5 to the pre-build CMake command so
   the library configures with newer CMake without modifying its source.

Signed-off-by: True Loan <tloan@phytec.com>
